<title>USA: U.S. chain store leading indicator up 0.4 pct -BTM.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store leading indicator up 0.4 pct -BTM.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi/Chain Store Age leading indicator of chain store sales rose 0.4 percent in the week ended December 7, the bank said.</p>
<p>The indicator's index rose to 313.3, a 0.1 percent rise year-over-year.</p>
<p>The indicator has about a seven-month lead time, BTM said.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
